  "verbalization": "Avanafil, an erectile dysfunction (ED) treatment, is linked to Premature Ejaculation (PE) through a series of indications. The evidence suggests that Avanafil may exert a role in the pathophysiology of PE by influencing ED-related pathways. Specifically, Avanafil is indicated for Erectile Dysfunction, which is associated with Alprostadil and Tadalafil, both of which are also used for ED. These medications are known to affect smooth muscle relaxation and blood flow, which could potentially influence ejaculatory control. The indirect pathway from Avanafil to PE implies a possible mechanism where ED treatments may inadvertently impact ejaculatory function, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a plausible but not definitively established link, highlighting the need for further research to clarify the relationship.",
